There are several ways to summarize a passage using Java code, including using NLP libraries like OpenNLP or Stanford CoreNLP, or using machine learning algorithms like KMeans clustering or Latent Dirichlet Allocation to extract the main topics and generate a summary based on that.
For this particular passage, a simple approach using NLP libraries like OpenNLP or Stanford CoreNLP would be effective. These libraries can identify the most important sentences and extract the key phrases and concepts to generate a summary.
Here's an example Java code using OpenNLP to summarize the passage:
```
import opennlp.tools.sentdetect.SentenceDetectorME;
import opennlp.tools.sentdetect.SentenceModel;
import java.io.FileInputStream;
import java.io.InputStream;
public class Summarizer {
    public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {
        // Load sentence detection model
        InputStream modelIn = new FileInputStream("en-sent.bin");
        SentenceModel model = new SentenceModel(modelIn);
        SentenceDetectorME sentenceDetector = new SentenceDetectorME(model);
        // Input passage
        String passage = "The world of technology is a rapidly changing one. In the past, computers and other tech were much less advanced than they are today.";
        // Detect sentences
        String[] sentences = sentenceDetector.sentDetect(passage);
        // Generate summary
        String summary = sentences[0] + " " + sentences[1];
        // Print summary
        System.out.println(summary);
    }
}
```
This code uses OpenNLP to detect sentences in the input passage and generates a summary by selecting the first two sentences.
Of course, this is just a simple example and may not work well for longer or more complex passages. In those cases, using machine learning algorithms like KMeans clustering or Latent Dirichlet Allocation may be more effective for generating a summary.

