What is the formula to calculate the minimum number of cards needed to ensure that each player in a 4-player game of 5-card draw has a unique set of cards? 
Assuming there are n cards in the draw pile, the number of unique combinations of 5 cards that can be dealt is given by the formula: 
nC5 = n! / (5!(n-5)!) 
To ensure that each player has a unique set of cards, we need to ensure that the number of unique combinations of 5 cards is greater than or equal to the number of players: 
nC5 >= 4 
Simplifying this inequality: 
n! / (5!(n-5)!) >= 4 
n! / (5! (n-5)!) >= 4/1 
n! / (5! (n-5)!) >= 4 
n! / (5! (n-5)!) - 4 >= 0 
We can solve this inequality numerically using JavaScript code:
let n = 1;
while ((factorial(n) / (factorial(5) * factorial(n-5))) - 4 < 0) {
  n++;
}
console.log("The minimum number of cards needed is: " + n);
function factorial(num) {
  let result = 1;
  for (let i = 2; i <= num; i++) {
    result *= i;
  }
  return result;
}
This code will iterate through increasing values of n until the inequality is satisfied, and then output the minimum value of n.

